    "narrative": "Our primary offensive anchor today is **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 77.96 score. Even without a confirmed opposing starter, his favorable home park profile and premium spot in the two-hole make him a must-start staple. He is joined in the top tier by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.94) and **Kyle Tucker** (67.63). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Mitch Keller, bolstered by a strong 0.378 xwOBA, while **Kyle Tucker** leverages a consistent performance floor against Brandon Sproat. We are also tracking **Jackson Merrill** (61.41) and **Andy Pages** (60.07) as key secondary contributors; **Jackson Merrill** enjoys a 13% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Luis Medina, while **Andy Pages** maintains steady value despite a slight penalty for playing against a pitcher who limits stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Nolan Schanuel** on the bench. His 53.06 score was competitive, but he was ultimately edged out by **Coby Mayo** (54.35) and **Liam Hicks** (52.50). While **Nolan Schanuel** offers reliability, **Coby Mayo**\u2019s significant park-factor advantage provided the necessary ceiling to round out the utility spot. Conversely, **Gage Workman** carries the highest risk among our starters; his 42.74 score is dampened by a platoon disadvantage against Trevor Rogers, making him a marginal play today. We are proceeding with caution given that all lineups are currently pending; should **Liam Hicks** or any other core piece be shuffled down the order, their efficiency scores will likely regress, necessitating a potential shift toward the high-contact profile of **Brayan Rocchio**, who remains our top bench pivot.",
